[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2642715812","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102522#issuecomment-2642715812","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102522","id":2642715812,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6dhKSk","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-07T11:50:21Z","updated_at":"2025-02-07T11:50:21Z","body":"Not sure if this is a bug, `is_script_supported` returns font metadata, so if font have flag for Latin set, it will assume it's supported. It's likely set, since some of the characters from these blocks are present (punctuation, $ sign).\n\n<img width=\"887\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8ef8c2fe-0a15-44bb-9db6-021db8635908\" />","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2642715812/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2642748611","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102522#issuecomment-2642748611","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102522","id":2642748611,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6dhSTD","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-07T12:08:15Z","updated_at":"2025-02-07T12:08:15Z","body":"And I'm not sure if there's a 100% reliable way to check it, since a lot of usable fonts only have subsets of script, we can check if specific text can be displayed by font (but this is a fallback system already doing), but not scrip in general. Checking for all characters in belonging to a specific script also won't work, since a lot of scripts have obscure, rarely used extensions. I'm pretty sure none of the font support `Latin Extended-G` block, so you can argue that there are no fonts with full Latin supports at all.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2642748611/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2642796478","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102522#issuecomment-2642796478","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102522","id":2642796478,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6dhd--","user":{"login":"lostminds","id":17763524,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NzYzNTI0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17763524?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds","html_url":"https://github.com/lostminds","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-07T12:32:14Z","updated_at":"2025-02-07T12:32:14Z","body":"> Not sure if this is a bug, `is_script_supported` returns font metadata, so if font have flag for Latin set, it will assume it's supported. It's likely set, since some of the characters from these blocks are present (punctuation, $ sign).\n\nI assumed it would look at some specified [script tags](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OpenType#Script_tags), but it seems these tags are only available in OpenType fonts and not in TrueType or PostScript fonts (?) which could explain why it's not working as well there. This begs the question then what the macOS Font manager is basing the script and language support information on for these TrueType fonts... Maybe they've added some meta-data of their own in the font system since these are system fonts used for these scripts/languages. \n\nSo it could be that it's falling back to looking for the presence of characters in different latin character sets. But if it's returning true just for containing some latin punctuation characters that still doesn't seem like the expected result regarding \"supporting the script\", as I'd expect this to mean at least supporting rendering a common text in this script. Just checking for the first letter in the script alphabet would probably work in most cases to avoid \"latin\" punctuation support cases. \n\nHowever, this would not explain the false negatives, fonts like Thonbury in the example above obviously has latin characters but still returns false on is_script_supported(\"Latn\"). So there may be something more going on. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2642796478/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2642817998","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102522#issuecomment-2642817998","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102522","id":2642817998,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6dhjPO","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-07T12:44:07Z","updated_at":"2025-02-07T12:44:07Z","body":"> I assumed it would look at some specified [script tags](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OpenType#Script_tags), but it seems these tags are only available in OpenType fonts and not in TrueType or PostScript fonts (?) which could explain why it's not working as well there.\n\nIt was checking OT script tags as well, but almost no font (even OpenType fonts) support them.\n\n> This begs the question then what the macOS Font manager is basing the script and language support information on for these TrueType fonts...\n\nProbably just checking if sample text used as preview for each language can be displayed with the font (after filtering out stuff that is not marked as supported in the metadata), it should be good enough to estimate what's supported.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2642817998/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2642822045","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102522#issuecomment-2642822045","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102522","id":2642822045,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6dhkOd","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-07T12:46:24Z","updated_at":"2025-02-07T12:46:24Z","body":"> It was checking OT script tags as well\n\nActually still checked, but as an addition to OS/2 metadata.\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/3f56b3b23916ff54a1715cb8444304ce3c50283d/modules/text_server_adv/text_server_adv.cpp#L1525-L1535","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2642822045/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2648450935","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102522#issuecomment-2648450935","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102522","id":2648450935,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6d3Cd3","user":{"login":"khaledhosny","id":93914,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkzOTE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/93914?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/khaledhosny","html_url":"https://github.com/khaledhosny","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khaledhosny/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khaledhosny/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khaledhosny/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khaledhosny/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khaledhosny/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khaledhosny/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khaledhosny/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khaledhosny/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khaledhosny/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-10T15:45:24Z","updated_at":"2025-02-10T15:45:24Z","body":"AFAIK, FontBook (or the relevant macOS API) use CLDR exemplar data to check language and script coverage. A while ago I wrote a Python script that use ICU to get language and script coverage and back then it seemed to match what FontBook reports:\nhttps://gist.github.com/khaledhosny/7c120b9795edb11dca9e12287cdb3b10\n\nApple might possibly be also checking `meta` table.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2648450935/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]